messages:
maya: paging: automated surge alert just fired for /v1/generate — p95 latency spiked and a subset of customers seeing 429s. Incident bot: Incident#512 created, severity=P2. assigning oncall

eli: seeing a tight window of sustained token rate from a small customer cohort, pattern looks like batching abuse + one long-running stream. logs: `client_id=acct_9f3, route=/v1/generate, token_rate=~1.8M/min`

ravi: ack, checking quota dashboard + shaper. i'm going to apply a temporary soft-quota at the edge for noisy callers (drop to 60% of baseline) and enable circuit-breaker on the stream gateway for >30s active streams. will post changes and ETA

opsbot: action: applied edge soft-quota policy `edge.soft_quota=0.6` to route /v1/generate region=us-west-2 (effective now).

maya: thanks. customer impact: some will see 429s or degraded throughput; CS notified. Jana, can you confirm top 3 customers impacted and whether any are enterprise with dedicated capacity?

jana-cs: confirmed — acct_9f3 (PLG but high traffic), acct_epsilon (trial org; automated load test), acct-enterprise42 (dedicated but using hosted fallback; flagged). I messaged enterprise42 rep and recommended they switch to dedicated pool pin to avoid noisy-host interference.

eli: on SDK guidance — we should send short-term instructions for clients: 1) respect 429 + Retry-After header 2) implement exponential backoff with jitter 3) use idempotency keys for non-idempotent calls 4) prefer small streaming windows and checkpointing

maya: drafting quick advisory. include code snippets for exponential backoff and idempotency header usage. also ask them to reduce concurrent open streams to <= 6 per API key.

eli: suggested snippet (node):

```js
// exponential backoff w/ full jitter
async function retryWithBackoff(fn, attempts = 6) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); } catch (err) {
      if (!shouldRetry(err) || i === attempts - 1) throw err;
      const base = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** i, 30000);
      const sleep = Math.random() * base;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, sleep));
    }
  }
}
// include an idempotency key for non-idempotent operations
fetch('/v1/generate', { headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': uuid() } })
```

ravi: ops note: for server-side mitigation I applied these live actions: 1) soft-quotas at edge (as opsbot said) 2) stream-duration circuit breaker (30s threshold) 3) disabled server-side prefetch for /v1/generate to reduce burst amplification 4) turned on token-prefetch window shrinking (from 1024 -> 512) for the hot model variant. Took ~45s to converge across nodes.

maya: good. will add these specifics to advisory so SDK teams can correlate. Also include the exact 429 behavior: we are returning `Retry-After` in seconds and a `x-rate-limit-reset` header with unix seconds.

eli: additional client guidance: - if you get 429, backoff and retry with idempotency key; - for streaming, resume from last checkpoint rather than restarting entire stream; - if your use case tolerates lower quality, use the quantized cheaper model alias we exposed `model://redwood-lite-v2` as fallback; instruct clients to prefer it under high-throttle signals.

jana-cs: sending tailored notes to impacted customers now. message to enterprise42: suggest pin to dedicated and provide rollback timing. to acct_9f3: ask them to reduce their worker concurrency and enable idempotency keys.

maya: handoff for next oncall (ravi leaving in 20): summary for next shift: "Incident#512: surge causing p95 latency and 429s on /v1/generate. Mitigations applied: edge soft-quota (0.6), stream circuit-breaker (30s), disabled prefetch, token window shrink. Clients: implement exponential backoff w/ jitter, idempotency keys, reduce concurrent streams to <=6, consider fallback to model://redwood-lite-v2. CS outreach in progress."

ravi: also include runbook refs: `/runbooks/traffic-mitigation` and `/runbooks/streaming-circuit-breaker` (link posted in thread). I've added a flag to rollback soft-quota if we see errors >5% other than 429.

opsbot: note: telemetry probe shows error-rate dropping from 7.2% -> 1.9% over last 4m. token throughput stabilized.

maya: ok, reduce pager from P2 to watch after 30m if no regression. leave incident open for tracking and customer follow-up. next oncall, escalate to P1 if any enterprise dedicated pool sees abnormal tail latency or loss.

eli: last quick docs we should publish to public SDK repo: - recommended retry policy (max attempts, base backoff, max backoff, jitter) - idempotency examples for python/java/js - how to detect server-enforced throttling via headers - streaming resume patterns. I'll open a PR to sdk-examples repo and link here.

jana-cs: I've sent the follow-ups to customers and will update hooks if anyone requests a quota uplift or dedicated handoff.

maya: thanks team. leaving detailed notes in incident ticket. ravi — safe handoff.

ravi: handoff ack. leaving pager with maya for 20m then jumping off.

opsbot: incident#512 updated: status=mitigated; next-review=2490015960."
